/*!
    \qmlmodule VSMM.ModListModel
    \title VSMM.ModListModel QML Module
    \brief Source list model of the installed mods.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype ModListModel
    \nativetype vsmm::ModListModel
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.ModListModel
    \brief List model with one row per installed mod.

    \l [QML] {ModSortFilterModel} sorts and filters this model. ModListModel
    has no properties or methods of its own, it defines the roles of each
    row:

    \table
    \header \li Role \li Type \li Description
    \row \li \c modId \li string \li Mod id.
    \row \li \c modName \li string \li Display name.
    \row \li \c modAuthor \li list<string> \li Authors.
    \row \li \c modVersion \li string \li Installed version.
    \row \li \c modLatestVersion \li string \li Version of the available update. Only meaningful when \c modHasUpdate is \c true, otherwise \c 0.1.0.
    \row \li \c modHasUpdate \li bool \li An update is available.
    \row \li \c modTags \li list<string> \li Tags from the online info.
    \row \li \c modUrl \li url \li Page of the mod on mods.vintagestory.at.
    \row \li \c modSide \li string \li The \c side field of the online info, for example \c both. Empty until the online info arrives.
    \row \li \c modThumbnail \li string \li \c modicon image URL, empty while the online info has no logo URL.
    \row \li \c isFavoriteMod \li bool \li The mod is a favorite.
    \row \li \c isMarkedForUpdate \li bool \li The mod is marked with \l {ModStore::markForUpdate()}{ModStore.markForUpdate()}.
    \endtable

    A delegate can read the roles unqualified:

    \qml
    Label { text: modName }
    \endqml

    \qml
    Rectangle { visible: modHasUpdate }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \qmlmodule VSMM.ModSortFilterModel
    \title VSMM.ModSortFilterModel QML Module
    \brief Sorted and filtered model of the installed mods.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype ModSortFilterModel
    \nativetype vsmm::ModSortFilterModel
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.ModSortFilterModel
    \brief Sorted and filtered proxy over \l [QML] {ModListModel}.

    It has the same roles as \l [QML] {ModListModel}. Rows are sorted by
    \c modName, ascending and case insensitive.

    \qml
    ListView {
        model: ModSortFilterModel
    }
    \endqml

    \qml
    TextField {
        onTextChanged: ModSortFilterModel.setFilterText(text)
    }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModSortFilterModel::setFilterText(string text)
    Keeps only the rows whose \c modName contains \a text, case insensitive.
    Author, tags and id are not searched. The text is matched literally, so
    regular expression characters have no special meaning. An empty string
    accepts every row.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmodule VSMM.ModUpdateModel
    \title VSMM.ModUpdateModel QML Module
    \brief Progress of the current mod update batch.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype ModUpdateModel
    \nativetype vsmm::ModUpdateModel
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.ModUpdateModel
    \brief List model with one row per mod of the current update batch.

    A batch starts when \l [QML] {ModStore} begins an update.
    Rows stay in the model after their mod finishes. A finished batch is
    removed by \l clear() or replaced when the next batch starts.

    \table
    \header \li Role \li Type \li Description
    \row \li \c modId \li string \li Mod id.
    \row \li \c modName \li string \li Display name.
    \row \li \c fromVersion \li string \li Installed version.
    \row \li \c toVersion \li string \li Version being installed.
    \row \li \c updateState \li enumeration \li One of the State values below.
    \row \li \c progress \li real \li Between \c 0 and \c 1, or \c -1 while downloading with an unknown size.
    \row \li \c errorText \li string \li Failure reason, empty unless \c updateState is \c Failed.
    \endtable

    The \c updateState role uses these values:

    \value ModUpdateModel.Queued No download progress has arrived yet.
    \value ModUpdateModel.Downloading The new zip is downloading.
    \value ModUpdateModel.Installing The new zip is moving into the mods folder.
    \value ModUpdateModel.Done The update finished.
    \value ModUpdateModel.Failed The update stopped, see \c errorText. A mod that is still unfinished when loading ends gets \c {Update ended without a result}.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModUpdateModel::count
    \readonly
    Number of mods in the batch.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModUpdateModel::finishedCount
    \readonly
    Number of mods in the \c Done or \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModUpdateModel::failedCount
    \readonly
    Number of mods in the \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty real ModUpdateModel::totalProgress
    \readonly
    Progress of the whole batch between \c 0 and \c 1. Finished mods count as
    complete, downloads with an unknown size count as \c 0.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool ModUpdateModel::active
    \readonly
    \c true while at least one mod is not \c Done or \c Failed.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModUpdateModel::clear()
    Removes all rows of a finished batch. Does nothing while \l active is
    \c true.
*/
